// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`screen: 'help partner options' > en 40 color 1`] = `
"  bladecp partner options
 ━━━━━━━━━━━━──────────────────────────
  The configurable options of your
  plans (memory, disk, extras), with
  their values and prices. Without
  --plan, every option of the account.

  Usage ────────────────────────────────
  bladecp partner options [--plan <id>]
      [--currency <code>]

  Options ─────────────────────────────
  --plan <id>
    Only the options of this plan: its
    ID or UUID from "bladecp partner
    plans"
  --currency <code>
    Show prices in one currency only
    (for example BRL or USD)

  Pick a value with --option
  <option>=<value> in "bladecp partner
  servers create" and "bladecp partner
  servers options". The label or the ID
  of a value works too.

  Examples ────────────────────────────
  › bladecp partner options
    Every option of the account
  › bladecp partner options --plan 12
    --currency BRL
    The options of plan 12, priced in
    BRL

  Global options ──────────────────────
  --json
    Print machine-readable JSON (no
    colors, no prompts)
  --api-url <url>
    API address (default
    https://api.bladecp.com)
  --lang <en|pt-BR|es>
    Language for messages
  --debug
    Describe each request on stderr
    (the key is never shown)
  --verbose
    Same as --debug
  -h, --help
    Show help
  -v, --version
    Show the version

  See also  bladecp partner servers
  create · bladecp partner servers
  options

